30,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The costs are higher than I expected. We are paying for empty space, and every single desk move costs us over 6,000 yen.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that the noise is much louder near the printer. Also, the physio said it takes a long time to get the chair and desk just right.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,Here's the kicker: the pilot floor spends up to nine minutes just setting up every morning. That's a total waste of time.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"My findings are quite telling. We have a few ""premium"" window seats and a few ""dungeon"" seats. Plus, our history of shuffles is a chaotic mess.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I found that sitting near people who work on different things actually helps. The new joiners learned a lot just by overhearing others.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, if the pilot floor is wasting time, we should avoid their setup. @Minato, if the printer is noisy, we should keep it away from the main cluster.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Minato,,"Yes, please. And since it takes so long to adjust the chairs, I think we should avoid moving seats too often. It's hard on the body.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly! I can't stand the idea of losing ten minutes of my morning to cable management. We need a fixed, efficient layout.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Fixed layouts are great for efficiency, but they're terrible for fairness. If we fix the seats, someone is permanently stuck in the ""dungeon.""","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"But... if we fix them, we can choose who sits together. If we put different projects near each other, we might learn more.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"We cannot afford a ""chaotic mess"" of shuffles. The facilities quote proves that frequent changes are a financial drain on our limited budget.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I agree with Victoria. Moving too much is expensive, and it's also tiring to have to fix your chair every time you move.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"See? We're all agreeing. No more ""hot-desking"" or random shuffles. I want to walk in and start working immediately.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,You're all prioritizing convenience and cost over the fact that some of you will be sitting in the dark. That's a recipe for resentment.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"Maybe... maybe we can just be careful about who we put in the dark? If we talk about it, it might be okay.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,We must prioritize a low-maintenance solution. A fixed layout that minimizes facilities costs and maximizes space usage is the only rational path.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Minato,,I just want to make sure that whoever sits in the noisy spot is okay with it. I don't think I could focus there.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"Let's just make sure we don't implement any ""morning rituals"" that eat into our gaps. I'm voting for whatever is fastest.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll agree to a fixed layout only if we have a transparent way to decide who takes the bad seats. No ""habitual"" assignments.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I think... as long as we aren't isolated, a fixed layout could be good. It gives us a chance to actually get to know the person next to us.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
