60,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Option A is the only viable choice. It minimizes facilities costs and avoids the daily time waste May mentioned.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I like Option A too. If the seats are fixed, I can spend the time to make my chair and monitor perfectly comfortable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,Option C is a nightmare. I'm not spending nine minutes every morning playing musical chairs with my laptop. I vote A.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A is a disaster for morale unless we rotate. Option B is the only way to ensure that the ""dungeon"" seats are shared fairly.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm worried about Option C. I think I'd just sit in the same spot and not talk to anyone. I prefer A or B.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, Option B would mean paying the facilities quote for every single person every time we rotate. We simply don't have the budget for that.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Minato,,"And the physio's note... if we rotate, we have to spend days adjusting the chairs again. That sounds very tiring.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,Exactly. Why would we intentionally create a system that wastes time and money? Option B is just Option C with a slower schedule.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Because Option A creates a caste system. The ""window people"" and the ""wall people."" If we don't rotate, we're just ignoring the inequality.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I think... if we use Option A, we can just... be kind to the people in the wall seats? Maybe we can put the most social people there?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Victoria,,Kindness doesn't pay the facilities bill. We have to be realistic. Option A is the most cost-effective and stable solution for the team.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Minato,,I agree. I think stability is more important than perfect fairness. I really need a spot where I can just... be.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"I'm with Victoria and Minato. My schedule is too tight for any ""rotation"" logistics or daily setup. Option A is the only one that respects our time.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"You're all choosing the path of least resistance. Fine. But if we go with A, I want it on the record that we're choosing convenience over fairness.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I think... Option A could actually be the best for us. If we're fixed, we can build real relationships with our neighbors.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Victoria,,It seems we have a consensus on the practical benefits. Let's move to the vote.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm happy as long as we can keep our settings. I'll vote for A.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I'm voting A. No more wasted mornings.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll vote B to stay consistent with my principles, but I can see the tide has turned.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll vote for A... I think it'll be easier for me to talk to people if I know where they are.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
